    {
      "wanneer": "2026-10-28T18:21:27+00:00",
      "gebeurtenis": "taal_na_skrywer",
      "punte": [
        "fix: [taal] in 'wanneer plekke ver van mekaar deel': 'plekke ver van mekaar deel van een wêreld word' is clipped, and a reader can stumble by reading 'ver van mekaar deel' together.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Party van die glasperle het uit Indië gekom. Hierdie lap is geweefde s': The sentence about the cloth sits between two sentences about the glass beads, so 'Hierdie lap' points back two sentences and 'daardie glasperle' has to jump over the cloth; moving the cloth sentence up to follow the block's first sentence would flow better, but that span holds a protected wording, so it is left for the writer.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Mense het van daardie glasperle later by Mapungubwe uit die grond gegr': 'later' is vague: a learner could read it as the people of Mapungubwe digging the beads up soon afterwards, while the next sentence implies a modern find (centuries later, by archaeologists); making that explicit would add content, so it is only flagged."
      ]
    },
